## 1. ARCHITECTURE PRINCIPLES
================================================================================

### 1.1 Domain-Driven Design (DDD) - MANDATORY
- Follow DDD patterns: Entities, Value Objects, Aggregates, Repositories, Domain Services
- Each microservice represents a bounded context
- NO cross-domain database access - use APIs or events
- Domain logic stays in domain layer, NOT in controllers or repositories
- Use Ubiquitous Language - domain terms must match business terminology

### 1.2 Layered Architecture (MANDATORY)
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Controller Layer (REST API)                                                │
│  - Input validation (DTOs)                                                  │
│  - HTTP concerns only                                                       │
│  - NO business logic                                                        │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Application Service Layer (Orchestration)                                  │
│  - Transaction management                                                   │
│  - Use case coordination                                                    │
│  - Cross-cutting concerns                                                   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Domain Layer (Business Logic) - PURE, NO FRAMEWORK DEPENDENCIES            │
│  - Entities & Value Objects                                                 │
│  - Domain Services                                                          │
│  - Business rules & invariants                                              │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Infrastructure Layer (Technical Concerns)                                  │
│  - Repository Implementations                                               │
│  - External API Clients                                                     │
│  - Messaging (Kafka)                                                        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 1.3 Microservices Uniformity
- All microservices MUST follow the same structure
- All CRUD operations follow the same pattern
- All error handling is consistent
- All logging is structured and uniform
- All configuration follows the same pattern

### 1.4 SOLID Principles (MANDATORY)
- **S**ingle Responsibility: One class = one reason to change
- **O**pen/Closed: Open for extension, closed for modification
- **L**iskov Substitution: Subtypes must be substitutable for base types
- **I**nterface Segregation: Many specific interfaces > one general interface
- **D**ependency Inversion: Depend on abstractions, not concretions

