## 4. NAMING CONVENTIONS (STRICT)
================================================================================

### 4.1 Packages
- Base: `com.foodai.{domain}` (e.g., `com.foodai.order`, `com.foodai.user`)
- Domain in lowercase, single word preferred

### 4.2 Classes
| Type              | Convention                    | Example                          |
|-------------------|-------------------------------|----------------------------------|
| Entity            | `{Name}`                      | `User`, `Order`, `Restaurant`    |
| Value Object      | `{Name}VO`                    | `AddressVO`, `MoneyVO`           |
| Enum              | `{Name}Status/Type`           | `OrderStatus`, `PaymentMethod`   |
| DTO Request       | `Create/Update{Name}Request`  | `CreateOrderRequest`             |
| DTO Response      | `{Name}Response`              | `OrderResponse`                  |
| Controller        | `{Name}Controller`            | `UserController`                 |
| Service           | `{Name}Service`               | `OrderService`                   |
| Domain Service    | `{Name}DomainService`         | `PricingDomainService`           |
| Repository        | `{Name}Repository`            | `UserRepository`                 |
| Mapper            | `{Name}Mapper`                | `OrderMapper`                    |
| Exception         | `{Name}Exception`             | `OrderNotFoundException`         |
| Event             | `{Name}Event`                 | `OrderCreatedEvent`              |
| Config            | `{Name}Config`                | `KafkaConfig`                    |

### 4.3 Methods
| Type              | Convention                    | Example                          |
|-------------------|-------------------------------|----------------------------------|
| CRUD Create       | `create{Entity}`              | `createOrder()`                  |
| CRUD Read (one)   | `findById`, `getById`         | `findById(id)`                   |
| CRUD Read (many)  | `findAll`, `findBy{Criteria}` | `findByUserId(userId)`           |
| CRUD Update       | `update{Entity}`              | `updateOrder(id, dto)`           |
| CRUD Delete       | `delete{Entity}`, `deleteById`| `deleteById(id)`                 |
| Boolean check     | `is{Condition}`, `has{Thing}` | `isActive()`, `hasPermission()`  |
| Business action   | `{verb}{Noun}`                | `processOrder()`, `cancelOrder()`|

### 4.4 Variables
- camelCase: `userId`, `orderTotal`, `restaurantName`
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE: `MAX_RETRY_COUNT`, `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE`
- Collections: plural nouns: `orders`, `items`, `users`

### 4.5 Database
| Database   | Tables/Collections | Columns/Fields  |
|------------|-------------------|-----------------|
| PostgreSQL | snake_case        | snake_case      |
| MongoDB    | camelCase         | camelCase       |

================================================================================
## 5. CRUD API STANDARDS (MANDATORY)
================================================================================

### 5.1 Endpoint Patterns
```
POST   /api/v1/{resource}              - Create
GET    /api/v1/{resource}/{id}         - Get by ID
GET    /api/v1/{resource}              - Get all (with pagination)
PUT    /api/v1/{resource}/{id}         - Update (full)
PATCH  /api/v1/{resource}/{id}         - Update (partial)
DELETE /api/v1/{resource}/{id}         - Delete
GET    /api/v1/{resource}/search       - Search with filters
POST   /api/v1/{resource}/{id}/{action}- Custom actions (e.g., /orders/{id}/cancel)
```

### 5.2 HTTP Status Codes (STRICT)
| Code | Meaning                  | When to Use                                |
|------|--------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| 200  | OK                       | Successful GET, PUT, PATCH                 |
| 201  | Created                  | Successful POST (return Location header)   |
| 204  | No Content               | Successful DELETE                          |
| 400  | Bad Request              | Validation errors, malformed request       |
| 401  | Unauthorized             | Authentication required                    |
| 403  | Forbidden                | Insufficient permissions                   |
| 404  | Not Found                | Resource not found                         |
| 409  | Conflict                 | Business rule violation (duplicate, etc.)  |
| 422  | Unprocessable Entity     | Semantic validation failure                |
| 429  | Too Many Requests        | Rate limiting                              |
| 500  | Internal Server Error    | Unexpected server errors                   |
| 503  | Service Unavailable      | Dependency failures                        |

### 5.3 Response Format (MANDATORY)
```json
// Success Response
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { /* entity or list */ },
  "timestamp": "2025-01-15T10:30:00Z",
  "requestId": "uuid",
  "path": "/api/v1/orders/123"
}

// Error Response
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "ORDER_NOT_FOUND",
    "message": "Order with id 123 not found",
    "details": [],
    "timestamp": "2025-01-15T10:30:00Z",
    "requestId": "uuid",
    "path": "/api/v1/orders/123"
  }
}

// Validation Error Response
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Validation failed",
    "details": [
      {
        "field": "email",
        "message": "Email is required",
        "rejectedValue": null,
        "code": "NotBlank"
      }
    ],
    "timestamp": "2025-01-15T10:30:00Z",
    "requestId": "uuid"
  }
}
```

### 5.4 Pagination (MANDATORY for list endpoints)
```
GET /api/v1/users?page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc

Response:
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "content": [ /* items */ ],
    "page": 0,
    "size": 20,
    "totalElements": 150,
    "totalPages": 8,
    "first": true,
    "last": false,
    "hasNext": true,
    "hasPrevious": false
  }
}
```

================================================================================
## 6. ERROR HANDLING (MANDATORY)
================================================================================

### 6.1 Exception Hierarchy
```java
// Business Exceptions (4xx errors)
BusinessException (extends RuntimeException)
    ├── ValidationException         // 400 - Invalid input
    ├── NotFoundException           // 404 - Resource not found
    ├── ConflictException           // 409 - Business conflict
    ├── UnauthorizedException       // 401 - Auth required
    ├── ForbiddenException          // 403 - Access denied
    └── UnprocessableEntityException// 422 - Semantic validation

// Technical Exceptions (5xx errors)
TechnicalException (extends RuntimeException)
    ├── DatabaseException           // 500 - DB errors
    ├── MessagingException          // 500 - Kafka errors
    ├── ExternalServiceException    // 503 - External API failures
    └── CacheException              // 500 - Redis errors
```

### 6.2 Global Exception Handler Requirements
- MUST have `@RestControllerAdvice` class
- MUST catch all exceptions and return standardized error response
- MUST log all errors with correlation ID
- MUST NOT expose stack traces in production
- MUST include request path in error response
- MUST use appropriate HTTP status codes

### 6.3 Exception Handling Pattern
```java
@RestControllerAdvice
@Slf4j
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    
    @ExceptionHandler(NotFoundException.class)
    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
    public ApiResponse<Void> handleNotFound(NotFoundException ex, WebRequest request) {
        log.warn("Resource not found: {}", ex.getMessage(), 
            kv("path", request.getDescription(false)),
            kv("errorCode", ex.getErrorCode()));
        return ApiResponse.error(ex.getErrorCode(), ex.getMessage());
    }
    
    // Handle all other business exceptions...
    
    @ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)
    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR)
    public ApiResponse<Void> handleGeneric(Exception ex, WebRequest request) {
        log.error("Unexpected error", ex,
            kv("path", request.getDescription(false)));
        return ApiResponse.error("INTERNAL_ERROR", "An unexpected error occurred");
    }
}
```

================================================================================
## 7. LOGGING STANDARDS (MANDATORY)
================================================================================

### 7.1 Log Levels
| Level | Usage                                                         |
|-------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| ERROR | Exceptions, critical issues requiring immediate attention     |
| WARN  | Recoverable errors, deprecated usage, rate limiting           |
| INFO  | Important business events (order created, user registered)    |
| DEBUG | Detailed diagnostic information (for development)             |
| TRACE | Very detailed diagnostic (method entry/exit, variable values) |

### 7.2 Structured Logging (JSON format - MANDATORY)
```java
// Use key-value pairs for structured logging
import static net.logstash.logback.argument.StructuredArguments.kv;

log.info("Order created successfully",
    kv("orderId", orderId),
    kv("userId", userId),
    kv("amount", amount),
    kv("correlationId", correlationId));
```

### 7.3 Required Fields in All Logs
| Field           | Description                              | Example                    |
|-----------------|------------------------------------------|----------------------------|
| timestamp       | ISO-8601 timestamp                       | 2025-01-15T10:30:00.123Z   |
| level           | Log level                                | INFO, ERROR, etc.          |
| logger          | Logger name                              | c.f.o.service.OrderService |
| message         | Log message                              | Order created successfully |
| correlationId   | Request correlation ID (MDC)             | uuid                       |
| spanId          | Distributed tracing span ID              | abc123                     |
| traceId         | Distributed tracing trace ID             | xyz789                     |
| serviceName     | Name of the microservice                 | order-service              |
| environment     | Deployment environment                   | prod, staging, dev         |

### 7.4 What NOT to Log
- Passwords, tokens, secrets
- Full credit card numbers
- Personal Identifiable Information (PII) - mask or hash
- Request/response bodies (unless DEBUG level and sanitized)

