## 8. TESTING REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY)
================================================================================

### 8.1 Coverage Thresholds (BLOCKING)
| Metric          | Threshold | Enforcement |
|-----------------|-----------|-------------|
| Line Coverage   | ≥ 80%    | JaCoCo      |
| Branch Coverage | ≥ 75%    | JaCoCo      |
| Method Coverage | ≥ 80%    | JaCoCo      |

### 8.2 Coverage by Layer
| Layer           | Line Coverage | Branch Coverage |
|-----------------|---------------|-----------------|
| Domain Model    | ≥ 90%        | ≥ 85%          |
| Services        | ≥ 85%        | ≥ 80%          |
| Controllers     | ≥ 80%        | ≥ 75%          |
| Mappers         | ≥ 80%        | ≥ 75%          |
| Repository      | ≥ 70%        | ≥ 65%          |

### 8.3 Test Types (ALL REQUIRED)

#### Unit Tests (JUnit 5 + Mockito)
- Test each method in isolation
- Mock all dependencies
- Fast execution (< 100ms per test)
- Test both happy path and edge cases
- Test all exception scenarios

#### Integration Tests (Spring Boot Test + Testcontainers)
- Test with real databases (Testcontainers)
- Test API endpoints end-to-end
- Test Kafka producers/consumers
- Use `@IntegrationTest` suffix

#### Controller Tests (MockMvc)
- Test all HTTP methods
- Test request validation
- Test response serialization
- Test error responses

#### Repository Tests (Testcontainers)
- Test custom queries
- Test pagination
- Test indexing effectiveness

#### Architecture Tests (ArchUnit)
- Enforce layered architecture
- Enforce package dependencies
- Enforce naming conventions

### 8.4 Test Naming Convention
```java
@Test
void shouldCreateUserSuccessfully_whenValidInput() { }

@Test
void shouldThrowNotFoundException_whenUserDoesNotExist() { }

@Test
void shouldReturnEmptyList_whenNoUsersExist() { }
```

### 8.5 Test Structure (AAA Pattern)
```java
@Test
void testName() {
    // Arrange - Setup test data and mocks
    User user = User.builder().id("1").name("John").build();
    when(userRepository.findById("1")).thenReturn(Optional.of(user));
    
    // Act - Execute the method under test
    UserResponse result = userService.findById("1");
    
    // Assert - Verify the results
    assertThat(result).isNotNull();
    assertThat(result.getName()).isEqualTo("John");
    verify(userRepository).findById("1");
}
```

### 8.6 Test Execution Rules
- **ALL tests MUST pass before code is considered complete**
- **Code coverage MUST meet thresholds**
- **No test should be @Disabled without JIRA ticket reference**
- **Tests MUST be deterministic (no flaky tests)**
- **Tests MUST be independent (no order dependency)**
- **Tests MUST clean up after themselves**

### 8.7 Mocking Best Practices
- Use `@Mock` for dependencies
- Use `@InjectMocks` for the class under test
- Use `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)`
- Verify interactions with `verify()`
- Use `ArgumentCaptor` for complex assertions

================================================================================
## 9. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY)
================================================================================

### 9.1 Authentication & Authorization
- Use JWT tokens for authentication
- Validate JWT in API Gateway
- Use `@PreAuthorize` for method-level security
- Implement role-based access control (RBAC)
- Never trust client-side data

### 9.2 Input Validation (Defense in Depth)
```java
// Controller Layer - DTO validation
public ResponseEntity<UserResponse> createUser(
    @Valid @RequestBody CreateUserRequest request) { }

// Service Layer - Business validation
public User createUser(CreateUserRequest request) {
    if (userRepository.existsByEmail(request.getEmail())) {
        throw new ConflictException("User with email already exists");
    }
    // ...
}
```

### 9.3 OWASP Top 10 Mitigations
| Vulnerability              | Mitigation                                    |
|---------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| Injection                 | Parameterized queries, input validation       |
| Broken Authentication     | JWT validation, secure session management     |
| Sensitive Data Exposure   | Encryption at rest/transit, masking PII       |
| XXE                       | Disable DTD processing                        |
| Broken Access Control     | RBAC, resource ownership validation           |
| Security Misconfiguration | Secure defaults, disable debug in prod        |
| XSS                       | Output encoding, Content-Security-Policy      |
| Insecure Deserialization  | Whitelist allowed classes                     |
| Components with Vulns     | OWASP Dependency Check, regular updates       |
| Insufficient Logging      | Structured logging, security event monitoring |

### 9.4 Secrets Management
- NEVER hardcode secrets in code
- Use environment variables or GCP Secret Manager
- Rotate credentials every 90 days minimum
- Use different credentials per environment
- Audit secret access

### 9.5 Data Protection
```java
// Sensitive data must be masked in logs
@ToString.Exclude
private String password;

@JsonIgnore
private String apiKey;

// Use encryption for sensitive fields
@Convert(converter = EncryptedStringConverter.class)
private String ssn;
```

