## 15. CI/CD REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

### 15.1 Pre-commit Checks (Local)
1. Code formatting (Spotless)
2. Static analysis (Checkstyle, SpotBugs, PMD)
3. Unit tests
4. Code coverage check

### 15.2 CI Pipeline Stages
```yaml
stages:
  - validate:        # Checkstyle, Spotless
  - compile:         # Maven compile
  - unit-test:       # Unit tests + coverage
  - static-analysis: # SpotBugs, PMD
  - security-scan:   # OWASP, Snyk, Trivy
  - integration-test:# Integration tests
  - sonar:           # SonarQube analysis
  - package:         # Build JAR
  - docker:          # Build & push image
  - deploy:          # Deploy to environment
```

### 15.3 Quality Gates (ALL MUST PASS)
| Gate                        | Threshold           | Blocking |
|-----------------------------|---------------------|----------|
| Code Coverage               | ≥ 80% line         | YES      |
| Branch Coverage             | ≥ 75%              | YES      |
| All Unit Tests Pass         | 100%               | YES      |
| All Integration Tests Pass  | 100%               | YES      |
| Code Smells                 | < 10               | YES      |
| Bugs                        | 0                  | YES      |
| Security Vulnerabilities    | 0 (Critical/High)  | YES      |
| Technical Debt Ratio        | < 5%               | YES      |
| Duplicated Lines            | < 3%               | YES      |
| Checkstyle Violations       | 0                  | YES      |
| SpotBugs Issues             | 0 (High/Medium)    | YES      |
| PMD Violations              | 0 (Critical)       | YES      |
| OWASP CVE Score             | < 7                | YES      |

### 15.4 Branch Protection Rules
- Require pull request reviews (minimum 2)
- Require status checks to pass
- Require conversation resolution
- Require signed commits
- No force pushes to main/develop

================================================================================
## 16. CRITICAL REMINDERS (MUST FOLLOW)
================================================================================

1. **NO CODE WITHOUT TESTS**: Every class must have corresponding test class
2. **80% COVERAGE MINIMUM**: Code coverage must be ≥ 80% line, ≥ 75% branch
3. **ALL TESTS MUST PASS**: No code is complete until all tests pass
4. **UNIFORM STRUCTURE**: All microservices follow the same structure
5. **DDD PRINCIPLES**: Domain logic in domain layer, not in controllers
6. **ERROR HANDLING**: Use exception hierarchy, never swallow exceptions
7. **LOGGING**: Structured logging with correlation ID, no sensitive data
8. **DOCUMENTATION**: JavaDoc + OpenAPI documentation mandatory
9. **SECURITY**: Validate all inputs, never trust client data
10. **PERFORMANCE**: Use caching, pagination, and async where appropriate
11. **CODE REVIEW**: All PRs require 2 approvals
12. **NO SECRETS IN CODE**: Use environment variables or secret managers
13. **IDEMPOTENCY**: All event handlers must be idempotent
14. **MONITORING**: Expose health, metrics, and tracing endpoints

================================================================================
## 17. CODE GENERATION CHECKLIST
================================================================================

When generating code for a microservice, verify ALL items:

### Phase 1: Domain Layer
- [ ] Domain entities with proper annotations
- [ ] Value objects (immutable)
- [ ] Enums for status/type fields
- [ ] Repository interfaces
- [ ] Domain services (if complex business logic)
- [ ] Unit tests for domain entities (≥90% coverage)

### Phase 2: Application Layer
- [ ] Application services with transaction management
- [ ] Input validation
- [ ] Error handling with proper exceptions
- [ ] Unit tests for services (≥85% coverage)

### Phase 3: API Layer
- [ ] REST controllers with proper annotations
- [ ] DTOs for request/response
- [ ] MapStruct mappers
- [ ] OpenAPI documentation on all endpoints
- [ ] Controller tests with MockMvc (≥80% coverage)
- [ ] Mapper tests (≥80% coverage)

### Phase 4: Infrastructure Layer
- [ ] Database configuration (Mongo/PostgreSQL)
- [ ] Redis configuration
- [ ] Kafka configuration
- [ ] External client configuration
- [ ] Repository tests with Testcontainers

### Phase 5: Cross-cutting
- [ ] Global exception handler
- [ ] Logging configuration (logback-spring.xml)
- [ ] Application configuration files (all profiles)
- [ ] Flyway migrations (if PostgreSQL)
- [ ] Health check endpoints

### Phase 6: Quality Gates
- [ ] Run `mvn clean verify` - ALL TESTS PASS
- [ ] Verify JaCoCo coverage ≥80% line, ≥75% branch
- [ ] Verify no Checkstyle violations
- [ ] Verify no SpotBugs issues
- [ ] Verify OpenAPI documentation complete
- [ ] Update service README
- [ ] Update DOMAIN_MODEL.md
- [ ] Update backend README.md

