## 22. QUALITY ENFORCEMENT SCRIPTS
================================================================================

### 22.1 Backend Master Validation Script

Location: `backend/mvnw.sh`

This is the master validation script that enforces all quality standards.

**Features:**
- Multi-mode validation (all, service, changeset, quick, full, cursor)
- Automatic Java 21 environment setup
- Comprehensive quality checks (compile, test, coverage, static analysis)
- Report generation (Markdown + detailed logs)
- Git-aware changeset detection
- Color-coded console output
- Non-zero exit code on failure (for CI/CD integration)

### 22.2 Usage Examples

```bash
# From backend/ directory

# Default: Validate changed services
./mvnw.sh

# Validate all services
./mvnw.sh all

# Validate specific service
./mvnw.sh service order-service

# Quick validation (tests only)
./mvnw.sh quick all

# Full validation with security scan
./mvnw.sh full all

# Cursor pre-completion validation
./mvnw.sh cursor

# Show help
./mvnw.sh help
```

### 22.3 Exit Codes

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| 0 | Validation PASSED |
| 1 | Validation FAILED |

### 22.4 Integration with CI/CD

```yaml
# GitHub Actions / Jenkins example
- name: Backend Validation
  run: |
    cd backend
    ./mvnw.sh all
  
- name: Upload Quality Report
  uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3
  with:
    name: quality-reports
    path: backend/target/quality-reports/
```

